# Prettier reflows Markdown. CLAUDE.md and AGENTS.md are hand-wrapped mirrors
# that must stay byte-identical, and a reflow rewrites both differently. The
# same rule already keeps ruff out of Markdown.
*.md

# Written by a tool, never by hand.
web/types/
pnpm-lock.yaml
pnpm-workspace.yaml
uv.lock
web/dist/
data/dist/

# The mcmeta snapshots of the extract tests, written by
# `tests/fixtures/build_block_tag_snapshot.py` with `json.dumps(indent=2)`.
#
# Two writers cannot own one file. Prettier keeps a short array on one line and
# `json.dumps` never does, so `pnpm format` reflows both files and the next
# rebuild writes them straight back. Without these rules `pnpm format:check`
# reports both files on a clean tree.
#
# The glob carries the version, because the file names do: a snapshot of the
# next Minecraft version arrives as `mcmeta_26_3_block_tags.json`, and a rule
# naming one version would let it through.
#
# The other files of `tests/fixtures/` stay formatted. A person wrote them, and
# they are small enough to read in a review.
tests/fixtures/mcmeta_*_block_tags.json
tests/fixtures/mcmeta_*_block_harvest.json
